        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3594ff03-642e-5eae-8e7a-a68e82d89a8a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Glorious Revolution, Wincanton Skirmish\n- Laws: Church Patronage (Scotland) Act 1711\n- Organizations: Church of Scotland\n- Roles: Patrons, noble patrons\n- People: James II of England, James VII of Scotland, William III, Prince of Orange\n\nFacts:\n- The Glorious Revolution, also called the Revolution of 1688, was the overthrow of King James II of England, who was James VII of Scotland, by a union of English Parliamentarians and the Dutch stadtholder William III, Prince of Orange.\n- The Wincanton Skirmish occurred on 20 November 1688 during the Glorious Revolution.\n- The Church Patronage (Scotland) Act 1711 was intended to let noble and other patrons in Scotland regain control over Church of Scotland parish churches.\n- The Church Patronage (Scotland) Act 1711 aimed to restore a custom that patrons had lost in the so-called Glorious Revolution.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
